        "title": "Duality - Weak, Strong, Complementary Slackness, Shadow Prices",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Every linear program (the **primal**) has a twin (the **dual**). The primal allocates resources to maximize value; the dual prices those resources to minimize the cost of \"buying them out.\" The two are bound by two theorems: **weak duality** (the dual always bounds the primal) and **strong duality** (at optimum, the bounds meet — *for LP, whenever a feasible optimum exists*). The dual variables are **shadow prices**: the marginal value of each constraint."
    }
